## 7. Pre-Flight Observability & Security Verification Checklist

Before opening a release Pull Request or promoting a build from Staging to Production, verify each verification item:

* **[ ] Datadog Client Token & Env:** Ensure client token is loaded from encrypted Bitrise build secrets, environment is properly tagged (`env:production` or `env:staging`), and service name matches `mobile-app-enterprise`.
* **[ ] Symbolication & Mapping Files Upload:** Bitrise pipeline step `datadog-upload-dsym` (iOS) and `datadog-upload-mapping` (Android) verified passing with zero missing symbol warnings.
* **[ ] Distributed Tracing Propagation:** Verify outbound HTTP headers contain valid `x-datadog-trace-id`, `x-datadog-parent-id`, and `x-datadog-sampling-priority=1` without leaking to unapproved third-party domains.
* **[ ] PII Masking Ingress Rules:** Confirm all input fields containing sensitive data (passwords, credit cards, SSN, tokens) use secure text entry to enforce Datadog automatic RUM text masking.
* **[ ] Soft & Hard Update Triggers:** Verify dynamic version response handles all 4 states (`ALLOWED`, `SOFT_UPDATE_OPTIONAL`, `HARD_UPDATE_REQUIRED`, `EMERGENCY_KILLSWITCH`) with active fallback if network is unreachable.
* **[ ] Push Notification Quotas:** Ensure all notification payloads dispatched by backend services conform to 4KB (FCM) and 4KB (APNs) limits, with strictly non-PII display content.
* **[ ] Apple Push Review Compliance:** Confirm the app does not condition primary features on push notification permission (Guideline 4.5.4) and provides in-app permission toggle.
* **[ ] Dual SSL Public Key Pinning:** Verify primary leaf and at least one unexpired backup leaf hash are configured. Confirm backup leaf is rotated if less than 60 days remain before expiry.
* **[ ] Task Switcher Snapshot Protection:** Background the application on physical test devices; confirm the OS task switcher displays a blurred window or blank placeholder with no cached PII visible.
* **[ ] Atomic Data Wipe Execution:** Trigger local wipe via diagnostic menu; confirm Keystore/Keychain master keys are permanently shredded and database files are zeroed from disk.





