## 5. Automated Crash Deobfuscation in Bitrise

Production Android binaries are shrunk and obfuscated using **R8/ProGuard**, while iOS binaries strip symbol tables into **dSYM archives**. Without deobfuscation files, stack traces in Datadog appear as unreadable machine code:

```text
# Obfuscated Stack Trace (Unreadable):
at a.b.c.d.a(SourceFile:42)
at com.enterprise.mobileapp.MainActivity.d(Unknown Source:12)

# Deobfuscated Stack Trace (With R8 Mapping / dSYM):
at com.enterprise.mobileapp.features.checkout.CheckoutViewModel.submitPayment(CheckoutViewModel.kt:184)
at com.enterprise.mobileapp.features.checkout.CheckoutFragment$onViewCreated$1.onClick(CheckoutFragment.kt:76)
```

### Automated Upload in Bitrise (`bitrise.yml`)
Add the official Datadog deobfuscation steps to your Bitrise release workflows:

```yaml
# =========================================================================
# Upload Android ProGuard / R8 mapping.txt to Datadog
# =========================================================================
- datadog-upload-proguard-mapping@0:
    title: Upload R8 Mapping to Datadog
    inputs:
      - client_token: $DATADOG_CLIENT_TOKEN
      - site: "datadoghq.com"
      - mapping_file_path: "android/app/build/outputs/mapping/release/mapping.txt"
      - service: "mobile-app-android"
      - version: $BITRISE_BUILD_NUMBER

# =========================================================================
# Upload iOS dSYM Debug Symbols to Datadog
# =========================================================================
- datadog-upload-dsym@0:
    title: Upload dSYM Archives to Datadog
    inputs:
      - client_token: $DATADOG_CLIENT_TOKEN
      - site: "datadoghq.com"
      - dsym_path: $BITRISE_DSYM_PATH
      - service: "mobile-app-ios"
      - version: $BITRISE_BUILD_NUMBER
```

