## 6. TGRC Privacy, PII Redaction & Security Masking

Compliance with enterprise security standards requires proactive data masking before packets leave the device:

<div class="portal-table-wrap">
  <table class="portal-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Data Category</th>
        <th>Examples</th>
        <th>Required Redaction Rule</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Authentication Headers</strong></td>
        <td><code>Authorization</code>, <code>Cookie</code>, <code>X-API-Key</code></td>
        <td>Strip or replace with <code>[REDACTED]</code> in all network resource attributes.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Input Text Fields</strong></td>
        <td>Passwords, Credit Card numbers, SSN</td>
        <td>Apply <code>MaskUserInput</code> on RUM text inputs; never capture sensitive field values.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>User Identity</strong></td>
        <td>Email address, Employee ID</td>
        <td>Pseudonymize using salted SHA-256 hashes: <code>setUser(id: sha256(employeeId))</code>.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Session Replay Privacy</strong></td>
        <td>Embedded WebViews, Bank routing numbers</td>
        <td>Apply <code>MaskAll</code> privacy mode; sensitive views display as blurred silhouettes.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

```typescript
// Enterprise User Identity Redaction Pattern
import { DdSdkReactNative } from '@datadog/mobile-react-native';
import { sha256 } from 'js-sha256';

export const setEnterpriseUserSession = (corporateEmail: string, tenantId: string) => {
  // Never pass raw email to Datadog!
  const hashedUserId = sha256(corporateEmail.trim().toLowerCase());

  DdSdkReactNative.setUser({
    id: hashedUserId,
    extraInfo: {
      tenant_id: tenantId,
      user_type: "corporate_employee",
      auth_method: "sso_saml"
    }
  });
};
```




