    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Tier 1: Allowed Version</strong></td>
        <td><code>current &gt;= min_supported</code> AND <code>current == latest</code></td>
        <td>Zero interruptions. The app launches immediately into the authenticated user flow.</td>
        <td>Standard production release operating within normal support SLAs.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Tier 2: Soft Update (Optional)</strong></td>
        <td><code>current &gt;= min_supported</code> AND <code>current &lt; latest</code></td>
        <td>A dismissible alert or banner displays with two options: <strong>"Update Now"</strong> (redirects to store) and <strong>"Skip / Later"</strong> (user continues using app).</td>
        <td>Incremental feature drops, non-critical UI polish, and minor performance upgrades.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Tier 3: Hard Update (Force Upgrade)</strong></td>
        <td><code>current &lt; min_supported</code></td>
        <td>A full-screen, non-dismissible blocking modal covers the app. The back button, swipe gestures, and deep links are disabled. A single button: <strong>"Update Required"</strong> redirects directly to Google Play or Apple App Store.</td>
        <td>Breaking API schema changes, sunsetted microservices, or patched high-severity security vulnerabilities.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Tier 4: Emergency Killswitch (Incident Mode)</strong></td>
        <td><code>emergency_killswitch.active == true</code> (Overrides all version checks)</td>
        <td>The app locks completely regardless of version number. All outgoing HTTP requests are aborted, in-memory auth tokens are wiped, and a full-screen maintenance message with status links is displayed.</td>
        <td>Zero-day active exploitation, major backend database outage, or global compliance shutdown.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
