## 1. OWASP MASVS Enterprise Compliance Matrix

Enterprise applications handling financial, agricultural trade, supply chain, or employee data must comply with the **OWASP Mobile Application Security Verification Standard (MASVS)**:

<div class="portal-table-wrap">
  <table class="portal-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>MASVS Category</th>
        <th>Security Requirement</th>
        <th>Enterprise Technical Implementation</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>MASVS-STORAGE</strong></td>
        <td>System credential storage &amp; PII hygiene</td>
        <td>Hardware-backed Android KeyStore (AES-256-GCM) and Apple Keychain (<code>kSecAttrAccessibleAfterFirstUnlockThisDeviceOnly</code>). Zero plain text in SharedPreferences or UserDefaults.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>MASVS-CRYPTO</strong></td>
        <td>Cryptographic algorithm standard</td>
        <td>Mandatory use of AES-GCM or ChaCha20-Poly1305 with random 96-bit initialization vectors (IV). Deprecated ciphers (DES, 3DES, MD5, SHA-1, ECB mode) are strictly banned.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>MASVS-NETWORK</strong></td>
        <td>Network transport security</td>
        <td>TLS 1.3 mandatory. Cleartext HTTP traffic disabled via <code>network_security_config.xml</code> and Apple App Transport Security (ATS). Public key pinning with active and backup hashes.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>MASVS-PLATFORM</strong></td>
        <td>Inter-Process Communication (IPC)</td>
        <td>Android components declare <code>android:exported="false"</code> unless explicitly whitelisted. WebViews disable <code>allowFileAccess</code> and JavaScript interfaces. Universal Links validate domains.</td>
