## 5. Screen Privacy &amp; App Switcher Masking (Anti-Shoulder Surfing)

When an employee switches apps or enters the multitasking carousel, the mobile operating system captures a high-resolution screenshot of the active screen. To prevent confidential customer data or pricing orders from being visible on the lock screen or carousel, applications must obscure sensitive views:

### Android: Hardware `FLAG_SECURE`
Setting `FLAG_SECURE` prevents the operating system from capturing screenshots, screen recordings, or caching thumbnails in the recent apps switcher:

```kotlin
// In MainActivity.kt onCreate():
override fun onCreate(savedInstanceState: Bundle?) {
    super.onCreate(savedInstanceState)
    window.setFlags(
        WindowManager.LayoutParams.FLAG_SECURE,
        WindowManager.LayoutParams.FLAG_SECURE
    )
}
```

### iOS: Multitasking Blur Overlay
When the application transitions from active to background state, overlay a visual blur effect over the key window:

```swift
// In AppDelegate.swift:
func applicationWillResignActive(_ application: UIApplication) {
    let blurEffect = UIBlurEffect(style: .dark)
    let blurEffectView = UIVisualEffectView(effect: blurEffect)
    blurEffectView.frame = window?.bounds ?? .zero
    blurEffectView.tag = 9999
    window?.addSubview(blurEffectView)
}

func applicationDidBecomeActive(_ application: UIApplication) {
    window?.viewWithTag(9999)?.removeFromSuperview()
}
